Here are some examples of custom URLs in Java, using different approaches:

**Using a custom class to represent the URL**
```java
public class CustomUrl {
    private String url;

    public CustomUrl(String url) {
        this.url = url;
    }

    public static CustomUrl constructUrl() {
        return new CustomUrl(Example.constructUrl());
    }
}

public static void main(String[] args) {
    CustomUrl customUrl = CustomUrl.constructUrl();
    System.out.println(customUrl.getUrl()); // prints "http://example.com"
}
```

**Using a StringBuilder to build the URL**
```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String url1 = Main.constructUrl1();
        String url2 = Main.constructUrl2();

        if (url1.equals(url2)) {
            System.out.println("Same URL: " + url1);
        } else {
            System.out.println("Different URLs: " + url1 + ", " + url2);
        }
    }

    public static String constructUrl() {
        return "http://example.com";
    }

    public static String constructUrl1() {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(Example.constructUrl());
        if (sb.length() > 20) {
            sb.append("...");
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }

    public static String constructUrl2() {
        return Example.constructUrl();
    }
}
```

**Using an if-else statement to conditionally build the URL**
```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String url1 = Example.constructUrl();
        String url2 = Example.constructUrl();

        if (url1.equals(url2)) {
            System.out.println("Same URL: " + url1);
        } else {
            System.out.println("Different URLs: " + url1 + ", " + url2);
        }
    }

    public static String constructUrl() {
        return "http://example.com";
    }
}
```

**Using Java's ternary operator to conditionally build the URL**
```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String url = Example.constructUrl() ? Example.constructUrl() : null;
        System.out.println(url != null ? url : "No URL constructed");
    }

    public static String constructUrl() {
        return "http://example.com";
    }
}
```
